# 12 October 2026: task M2, resynthesis of a transcribed score (score.json of M1) with the procedural sound bank.
# Rule of 12 October 2026 (Matthieu): everything, music included, is first reproduced 1:1 at 99 percent, procedurally,
# as a measurement benchmark; variations are then derived by changing parameters. No reference sample ever enters a
# render: the score gives notes and hits, the bank blocks give timbres fitted by dfit on isolated notes of each Demucs
# stem, and every other number (equaliser, stereo width, compressor, loudness) is a measured parameter.
# Pipeline (one version V_NNN per run, never overwritten, private):
#   1. roles: one per drum class and per tonal voice of score.json; candidates = ready bank blocks (index.json re-read
#      every run, filtered by role tags and ids) plus the M2 instruments (datasets/music-instruments, same contract).
#   2. exemplars: the K least overlapped louder notes of each role, cut from the role's stem (mid channel).
#   3. fits: dfit on each (candidate, exemplar), pitch and onset narrowed around the transcription; 16 processes.
#   4. choice: each fitted timbre is cross-rendered on the role's other exemplars; the best mean ploss score wins.
#   5. render (pure function of params.json and score.json): every note, role buses with their effects, per-section
#      third-octave equaliser, gain riding toward the score's automation lanes, decorrelated stereo, mix bus.
#   6. scores: ploss (full song and per bar), verify.report (mix and music), onset F, chroma, envelope correlation,
#      per-section spectral envelope, per stem and for the mix.
# 12 October 2026: a role whose spec carries engine "sms" is rendered by the measured timbre models of sms.py instead
# of a bank block; stems get a stochastic residual bed; score_stable adds plossEvents, plossBarNoOnset and tfBands.
# Parameters: datasets/resynth-params.json (HDA interface), --set a.b=json, ZRMD_RESYNTH_OVERRIDES.
# FR : resynthese de la partition M1 avec la banque son ; timbres ajustes par dfit, rendu pur depuis params.json.
